{
  "_comment": "Which of NYNJTC's paper maps covers what, as a join a person reviews row by row (#1574 - A hiker on NYNJTC ground has nowhere to buy the paper map for where they are). Three kinds of fact, each with its own source, and none of them measured by this project: `handle` and `title` are the store's product handle and title, read from store.nynjtc.org/collections/maps/products.json on 2026-09-17 (the store is Shopify, so a handle is the product's URL); `sheets` is the store's own list of sheet numbers in the product's description, cross-checked against the digital-maps page; `sheet_covers` is the per-sheet list of parks and trails NYNJTC publishes at nynjtc.org/digital-trail-maps-on-mobile-devices/, verbatim, read the same day - it is the key the hike-detail join matches a hike's park name against, so a name here is NYNJTC's spelling and never this project's paraphrase; `covers` adds the few park names the store's product description itself names, where it names any. `avenza` names the Avenza Map Store product that sells each sheet singly, which is where archive_nynjtc_sheet_extents.py read each sheet's georeferenced footprint ONCE - the footprints themselves are not in this file, deliberately: they are fetched numbers, and fetched numbers go in the bucket (archive/nynjtc_map_sheets.json), not in a commit (CONTRIBUTING.md, 'Data does not go in commits'). export_sources.py reads this file through sources.json's `nynjtc_store.paper_maps` and publishes it on the NYNJTC steward record. WHAT IS NOT HERE: a price. The store is the source for that and an offline phone showing a stale one would be the display outrunning its source.",
